There is an important distinction between the product's 30 named review stages and its actual execution. The source coordinates a deterministic preflight and a small number of substantial model passes. Many of the named stages are requested as sections within those model responses, rather than executed as independently verified stages.

That is not inherently wrong for an MVP, but it matters when the report presents the output as a thoroughly verified, 30-stage expert review.
