11. Implementation order
I would avoid a wholesale rewrite. The following sequence retains the existing work and corrects its most consequential weaknesses.

Phase 1 — Scientific integrity
Highest priority

Replace PDF extraction, preserve page coordinates, remove lossy context truncation, fix scoring, distinguish unverified findings and add source-evidence checks.

Exit condition: The psychiatric-bed paper no longer produces the false claims about meta-analysis or heterogeneity.




Phase 2 — Professional appraisal engine

Introduce study-design routing, independent counterevidence verification, a structured finding ledger, editorial reconciliation and clinical applicability assessment.

Exit condition: Every consequential finding can be independently traced and challenged.




Phase 3 — Report and UI redesign

Build the principal appraisal report and technical appendix; implement professional pagination, references, bookmarks and an evidence-inspection interface.

Exit condition: PDF exports pass automated layout checks and independent editorial review.




Phase 4 — Validation and release hardening

Develop benchmark papers across different research designs, protect credentials, migrate persisted data safely, introduce CI and document limitations.

Exit condition: Known error cases remain fixed across repeated releases, and the app's confidentiality controls are verified.



Minimum acceptance criteria for the psychiatric-bed benchmark
The complete original manuscript should be used as a regression fixture. The application should correctly extract its 2022 search cutoff, the 65 publications and 98 estimates, the random-effects analyses, the reported I², the quality-scoring approach and the independent extraction procedure.

It should also identify the potentially inconsistent long-stay confidence interval on page 8, relate it to Figure 2, and avoid inventing missing methods.

On the reporting side, the six-axis scores must reconcile with the displayed composite, severity must be consistent with the overall appraisal, and no text may be truncated or misplaced. The exported report should contain verifiable references and clearly disclose any materials that were not successfully inspected.

12. Final engineering judgment
The source-code review has changed my assessment in an important way.

Paper Critic's central problem is not that the AI needs to be made more intelligent or more aggressive. The app is currently denying the AI reliable access to parts of the paper, then allowing the resulting guesses to become authoritative findings.

The existing Kotlin implementation provides a useful foundation, including real deterministic checks, structured AI responses, native UI components, persistent reviews and PDF export. Those are worth preserving.

But the next version should enforce a clear hierarchy:
Complete source evidence
Correct methodological analysis
Independently verified findings
Coherent editorial judgment
Publication-grade presentation

If these five layers are implemented properly, the resulting report could be both exceptionally detailed and scientifically restrained.

My single highest-priority recommendation is to rebuild ManuscriptExtractor.kt and the evidence-verification path in Reviewer2PipelineService.kt before spending more effort on visual styling. That is where the largest improvement in professional credibility will come from.

Scope: This audit inspected the accessible repository source and both provided PDFs, including a reconstruction of the PDF extraction heuristic. It did not compile the Android application, execute live AI requests or modify the GitHub repository.